      "title": "Letterboxd review of Eureka",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Eureka\"] Wow.Wow. Wow. Wow.Eureka for its first three acts is one of the most amazing, bold, idiosyncratic epics I have ever seen. Then it has a fourth act, so incongruous to what has come before, it almost seems like a joke. Itself only adding to the overall oddness. For the first 90 minutes Eureka is to gold what There Will be Blood is to oil and Chinatown is to water. A virulent critique of untrammelled capitalism, through the eyes of pure ideology, that is something beyond mere greed. As Gene Hackman says about himself \"[i] used to have it all, but now I just have everything\".Hackman gives an incre",
      "link": "https://letterboxd.com/film/eureka/"
