      "title": "Letterboxd review of Eureka",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Eureka\"] I highly recommend you watch a different Nicolas Roeg film before you dive into Eureka. If only to get a sense of the director’s style which always feels like a surreal yet grounded experience. The film itself follows prospector Jack McCann, played by the legendary Gene Hackman as he strikes gold and then cuts to his life 20 years later which is strife with contention from a few different angles, including his own family and local mobsters who want to build a casino on his island. The films draws heavy parallels fo Citizen Kane and the madness you find yourself in when you have endless wealth.",
